# Update `/changelog` when work ships

User-facing Closeloop/Saidloop work is incomplete until the public changelog is updated.

## Source of truth

- Page: `/changelog` (`project/frontend/src/app/changelog/page.tsx`)
- Entries: `project/frontend/src/lib/changelog.ts` → `CHANGELOG_ENTRIES`
- Newest first. Shape: `{ date: "YYYY-MM-DD", title, body }` (ISO date, short title, 1–2 sentence body in English product voice).

## When to update

Before marking a task done (and before commit/push), **prepend** an entry if the change is user-visible:

- New or changed product features (API, MCP, widget, inbox, dashboard, auth, notify)
- Marketing/docs pages users can open (`/docs`, `/about`, `/contact`, landing, etc.)
- Notable fixes or behavior changes reporters/builders would notice

Same calendar day → prefer **one** entry that covers the day’s ship (expand title/body) instead of many tiny rows, unless the releases are clearly separate.

## Skip only when

- Cursor rules / agent config only
- Pure internal refactors, tests, or tooling with no user-visible change
- Typo/chore that does not change product behavior or public copy users care about
- Explicit user skip

```text
❌ Feature/UI/docs ship with no CHANGELOG_ENTRIES update
✅ Ship + prepend entry in changelog.ts (newest first) → /changelog reflects it
```
